    "designMd": "# Design System: Folio3 Parking\n\n## 1. Visual Theme & Atmosphere\nA dark, exact instrument for one building's car park. It should feel like the readout of a calibrated device, not a sci-fi console. Surfaces are near-black and tinted slightly towards a cool cyan, stacked in three steps. Depth comes from layered tints and 1px inset hairlines, never from shadows or glow. Every number, plate, floor, space code and timestamp is set in monospace with tabular figures. Labels are small, uppercase and tightly set. The single cyan accent shows up only as thin lines, small fills, the active indicator and the focus ring.\n\n- **Density 7 (Cockpit-leaning Balanced):** administrators and guards work at a desk all day, so tables are dense, calm and quick to scan. Employee screens on phones open up to a comfortable 44px+ touch rhythm.\n- **Variance 4 (Offset, grid-true):** left-aligned headers, a 12-column grid, content panels offset to columns 1–8 with a 4-column context rail. No centred hero layouts.\n- **Motion 7 (Fast and exact):** numbers roll to their value, bars and rules draw in, a shared element carries from a list into its detail, rows slide in with a short shift and one live element breathes.\n\n**What the field taught us, by product:**\n- **BMW:** crisp technical blue, sharp corners and restrained, mid-weight headings. We keep the sharpness and the technical calm.\n- **SeatGeek:** a bright cyan paired with deep navy-black. Our accent comes from this cyan family, toned down and shifted cooler for a dark UI.\n- **Tesla:** one colour, used only on the primary action, against neutral fields. The accent never decorates.\n- **Ticketmaster:** a ticket or pass whose key fact and code read at a glance. The parking pass leads with a large floor figure set in mono.\n\nField defaults we changed, and why: **mode** (light → dark, because guards and admins watch live screens for long sessions), **neutrals** (pure → accent-tinted), **density** (comfortable → dense tables) and **type** (all-sans → sans + mono for every figure).\n\n## 2. Color Palette & Roles\n**Surfaces (three tinted steps, never pure black)**\n- **Bay Black** (#0B1013) — app canvas, the deepest layer\n- **Deck Slate** (#11181C) — panels, table body, sheets\n- **Ramp Slate** (#182227) — raised layer: table header, selected row, inputs, popovers\n- **Inset Well** (#080C0E) — recessed areas: the camera frame, code blocks, the inside of progress tracks\n\n**Lines**\n- **Hairline** (rgba(196,232,240,0.08)) — default 1px dividers, panel borders, table rules\n- **Hairline Strong** (rgba(196,232,240,0.16)) — input borders, active panel edges, inset top rules on raised surfaces\n\n**Text**\n- **Signal White** (#E4ECEE) — primary text and figures\n- **Gauge Grey** (#8C9CA2) — secondary text, column headers, metadata\n- **Dim Grey** (#5D6C72) — tertiary text, disabled, placeholder\n\n**Accent (the only one)**\n- **Bay Cyan** (#36B0CC) — primary action fill, active tab indicator, focus ring, progress and utilisation lines, selected-row left rule, live dot. Saturation about 60%.\n- **On Cyan** (#061316) — text and icons placed on Bay Cyan fills (contrast above 8:1)\n- **Cyan Tint** (rgba(54,176,204,0.12)) — selected row background, pressed tint, accent badge background\n\n**Status (used only for entry results, alerts and validation, never decoration)**\n- **Granted Green** (#4FB286) — verified entry, success, active vehicle\n- **Hold Amber** (#D9A441) — pending, unverified, manual check needed, warnings\n- **Denied Red** (#E0564B) — rejected entry, errors, destructive actions such as reversing a claim\n- Each status is a 6px solid square plus a mono uppercase word. Colour is never the only signal.\n\n## 3. Typography Rules\n- **Display / Headings:** IBM Plex Sans, weight 500 (page titles) and 600 (section titles only). Tracking −0.02em. Page title size is clamp(1.5rem, 1.1rem + 1.4vw, 2.25rem). Hierarchy comes from weight and colour, not size jumps.\n- **Body:** IBM Plex Sans 400. 0.9375rem (15px) on desktop, 1rem on mobile. Line-height 1.55, max 65ch.\n- **Mono:** IBM Plex Mono 400/500 for every number, plate, floor, space code, time, date, count and CSV-style value. Always `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums slashed-zero`.\n- **Labels:** IBM Plex Mono 500, 0.6875rem (11px), uppercase, tracking +0.08em, colour Gauge Grey.\n- **Key figure:** IBM Plex Mono 500, clamp(3rem, 2rem + 5vw, 5.5rem), tracking −0.03em. Used for the one fact per screen (free-space count, floor on the pass).\n- **The one deliberate contrast:** case. Uppercase mono labels sit against sentence-case sans text. Width and weight stay steady.\n- **Craft:** curly quotes, en dash for ranges (08:00–18:30, 3–30 Oct), true ellipsis, dates such as \"Tue 14 Oct\" and 24-hour times.\n- **Banned:** Inter, Playfair Display, any serif, gradient text, display weights above 600.\n\n## 4. Component Stylings\n- **Buttons:** sharp 2px radius, height 40px desktop and 48px mobile.\n  - Primary: Bay Cyan fill with On Cyan text, max one per view.\n  - Secondary: transparent with a Hairline Strong border and Signal White text.\n  - Destructive: Denied Red border and text, filling red only in a confirm step.\n  - Press: `scale(0.97)` at 90ms. Hover: a trailing arrow icon nudges 3px, or the background steps one surface tint.\n  - No glow, no pulsing. Labels are product verbs (\"Release today’s space\", \"Claim space\", \"Record entry\", \"Export CSV\"), never \"Get started\".\n- **Panels (instead of cards):** Deck Slate on Bay Black with a 1px Hairline border and a 1px Hairline Strong inset top rule (`box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(196,232,240,0.16)`). Radius 2px. No drop shadows. Inside panels, sections are split with border-top hairlines, not nested boxes.\n- **Tables:** the main admin and guard surface.\n  - Row height 40px (36px compact).\n  - Header in Ramp Slate with mono uppercase labels. Sortable columns show a small caret.\n  - Number columns are right-aligned and tabular. Plates and codes use mono.\n  - Hover tints the row with Ramp Slate. A selected row gets Cyan Tint plus a 2px Bay Cyan left rule.\n  - The header row is sticky. Zebra striping is not used.\n- **Bay Plate:** every space code, floor and licence plate sits in a mono uppercase chip inside a 1px Hairline Strong frame, with a 2px left rule in Bay Cyan for the user’s own space. It echoes the painted line at a parking bay. See §11.\n- **Live count:** a large mono key figure, a mono label above it (\"FREE SPACES · 09:42\") and a thin 2px utilisation track under it that draws to its value.\n- **Pass / detail sheet:** Deck Slate panel with a perforation-style dashed hairline across it. The floor is set as the key figure, and plate, space and date are in Bay Plates. The final state shows a Granted Green square plus \"FINAL — CANNOT BE CANCELLED\" in mono.\n- **Inputs:** label above (mono uppercase label style), Ramp Slate fill, Hairline Strong border, 2px radius, 44px height. Focus ring: `outline: 2px solid #36B0CC; outline-offset: 2px`. Helper text below in Gauge Grey. Error text below in Denied Red with an icon. No floating labels. Plate inputs are mono uppercase.\n- **Tabs / segmented filters:** text tabs with a 2px Bay Cyan indicator that slides underneath.\n- **Status tags:** 6px colour square plus mono uppercase word, no pill backgrounds.\n- **Loaders:** skeleton bars in Ramp Slate with a slow shimmer, sized exactly to the rows and figures they replace. No spinners.\n- **Empty states:** one plain sentence saying what is missing and the single action that fills it (\"No vehicles yet. Add a plate to claim spaces.\"), with an outline Bay Plate drawn in Dim Grey as the illustration.\n- **Errors:** inline beside the cause. A recoverable error panel shows a plain cause, one retry button and the support contact in mono.\n- **Icons:** Lucide at stroke width 1.5, 16px in tables and 20px in navigation. Used only where they speed up recognition (camera, car, calendar, download, alert).\n\n## 5. Layout Principles\n- **Grid:** 12 columns, 24px gutters, max-width 1440px. Main content spans columns 1–8 or 1–12 for tables. A context rail on columns 9–12 holds filters, totals and selected-row detail.\n- **Chrome:** a left rail navigation (232px, Deck Slate, hairline right edge) for admin and guard roles. The nav is text-first with mono section labels. Employee roles get a top bar on desktop and a 3–4 item bottom bar on mobile.\n- **Page header:** a mono uppercase breadcrumb or label, then the title, with one primary action aligned right on the same baseline. No hero blocks.\n- **Spacing scale:** 4 / 8 / 12 / 16 / 24 / 32 / 48. Section gaps are clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem).\n- **Rhythm:** alternate a key-figure strip, a dense table and a narrow text column. Never repeat one template down a page.\n- **Responsive:**\n  - Below 768px everything collapses to one column and tables become stacked row-lists (primary value left, mono value right).\n  - Never scroll horizontally.\n  - Touch targets are at least 44px.\n  - The left rail collapses into a menu sheet.\n  - Full-height views use `min-h-[100dvh]`.\n- No overlapping elements and no absolute-positioned content stacking. CSS Grid for structure.\n\n## 6. Motion & Interaction\nMotion is fast, exact and always means something: a value arriving, a row being added, an item carried into its detail. Entrances are short, use 8–12px of travel at most and play once. Only `transform`, `opacity` and `clip-path` are animated. Full system in §9.\n\n## 7. Anti-Patterns (Banned)\n- No emojis, no Inter, no serif fonts, no pure black (#000000).\n- No glow, neon, outer shadows, gradient blobs, aurora backgrounds, glass blur or purple-to-blue gradients.\n- No pill badges above headers, no KPI-card rows with sparklines and green \"+12%\" chips, no 3 equal cards in a row, no bento grids.\n- No sparkle icons, no icons on every row, no stock photography, no illustrations of cars.\n- No generic names (\"John Doe\", \"Acme\"). Use realistic names (e.g. \"Hira Qureshi\", \"Usman Tariq\"), realistic plates (e.g. \"LEB-21-4471\") and odd real counts (e.g. \"17 of 64\").\n- No fake round metrics, no AI clichés (\"Seamless\", \"Elevate\", \"Unleash\").\n- No \"Scroll to explore\", no bouncing chevrons, no custom cursors.\n- No typewriter text, no pulsing buttons, no parallax, no scroll-jacking, no identical fade-up on every section, no animations that replay on every scroll pass.\n\n## 8. Voice & Font Rationale\n- **Voice:** exact, quiet, watchful.\n- **Display:** IBM Plex Sans. It was drawn for engineered, industrial contexts, and its squared curves and plain grotesk forms read like the labelling on an instrument panel, not a marketing page (fallback: Hanken Grotesk).\n- **Body / Mono:** IBM Plex Sans + IBM Plex Mono. They come from the same family, so text and figures share proportions. Plex Mono’s slashed zero and distinct 1/l keep plates and space codes unambiguous for a guard checking them quickly (fallback: Red Hat Mono).\n\n## 9. Motion System\n- **Tokens:** --dur-instant 90ms · --dur-quick 160ms · --dur-base 260ms · --dur-slow 420ms · --dur-scene 720ms · --ease-out cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1) · --ease-in cubic-bezier(0.7,0,0.84,0) · --ease-inout cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1) · --ease-spring linear(…) as below · --travel 8px (max 12px).\n- **Entrance (once per load, under 720ms):** the mono label, then the title, then the key figure and the first 6 table rows. Each fades in with an 8px rise, staggered 60ms. Rows after 6 appear together. The key figure rolls from 0 to its value over 600ms.\n- **Scroll-linked:** utilisation bars and report chart lines draw in (`scaleX` 0 → 1 from the left) as they enter (`animation-timeline: view(); animation-range: entry 0% entry 40%`), so each shows its share. They reveal once.\n- **Interaction feedback:**\n  - Buttons press with `scale(0.97)` at 90ms, and their arrow nudges 3px on hover at 160ms.\n  - Table rows tint to Ramp Slate at 160ms.\n  - Text links get an underline that draws from the left (scaleX 0 → 1).\n  - The focus ring appears instantly.\n  - Mobile list items show the Cyan Tint pressed state immediately on touch.\n- **State transitions:**\n  - The tab indicator slides at 260ms with --ease-inout.\n  - Accordions open via `grid-template-rows: 0fr → 1fr` at 260ms.\n  - New log or verification rows insert at the top with opacity 0 → 1 and an 8px downward shift at 160ms. The status square holds its colour.\n  - Sheets slide up at 420ms with --ease-out over a 40% backdrop.\n  - Screen pushes on mobile move 24px with a fade.\n  - Exits run about 30% faster with --ease-in.\n- **Ambient (max 1 per screen):** the live dot beside a real-time readout (the free-space count or the live entrance feed). An 8px Bay Cyan square sits still while a 1px ring scales 1 → 1.5 and fades 0.35 → 0 on a 6s cycle.\n- **Signature moment:** \"Bay carry-over.\" The Bay Plate of the chosen space carries from its list row into the parking pass through the View Transitions API (`view-transition-name: bay-plate`, 420ms, --ease-inout), and the floor key figure then rolls to its value in 600ms.\n- **Reduced motion:** entrances become instant opacity changes. The number roll, line draw and ambient ring are removed and values show at once. State changes keep at most a 120ms fade. Nothing is hidden waiting for an animation.\n\n```css\n:root{\n  --dur-instant:90ms;--dur-quick:160ms;--dur-base:260ms;--dur-slow:420ms;--dur-scene:720ms;\n  --ease-out:cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1);--ease-in:cubic-bezier(0.7,0,0.84,0);\n  --ease-inout:cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1);\n  --ease-spring:linear(0,0.009,0.035 2.1%,0.141,0.281 6.7%,0.723 12.9%,0.938 16.7%,1.017,1.077 21.4%,1.121 24%,1.149 27%,1.159,1.154 33%,1.051 43.2%,1.013 49.5%,0.996 57%,1.001 72%,1);\n  --travel:8px;\n}\n@keyframes rise{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(var(--travel))}to{opacity:1;transform:none}}\n@keyframes draw{from{transform:scaleX(0)}to{transform:scaleX(1)}}\n@keyframes row-in{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(-8px)}to{opacity:1;transform:none}}\n@keyframes live-ring{0%{transform:scale(1);opacity:.35}60%,100%{transform:scale(1.5);opacity:0}}\n.enter{animation:rise var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out) both;animation-delay:calc(var(--i,0)*60ms)}\n.bar{transform-origin:left;animation:draw var(--dur-slow) var(--ease-out) both;animation-timeline:view();animation-range:entry 0% entry 40%}\n.row-new{animation:row-in var(--dur-quick) var(--ease-out) both}\n.live-dot{position:relative;width:8px;height:8px;background:#36B0CC}\n.live-dot::after{content:\"\";position:absolute;inset:0;border:1px solid #36B0CC;animation:live-ring 6s var(--ease-inout) infinite}\n.bay-plate{view-transition-name:bay-plate}\n::view-transition-group(bay-plate){animation-duration:var(--dur-slow);animation-timing-function:var(--ease-inout)}\n.btn:active{transform:scale(.97);transition:transform var(--dur-instant) var(--ease-out)}\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){\n  *,*::before,*::after{animation:none!important;transition:opacity 120ms linear!important}\n  .live-dot::after{display:none}\n}\n```\n\n## 10. Component Substitutions\n- KPI cards with sparklines → one key figure with a timestamp, then a dense sortable table.\n- Feature cards with icons in squares → text-first panels split by hairlines.\n- Stats row \"99.9% / 24/7\" → real counts with their time window (\"17 of 64 free · 09:42\").\n- Glass or gradient backgrounds → three flat tinted surfaces with inset hairlines.\n- Pill status badges → a 6px colour square plus a mono uppercase word.\n- Icon on every nav link → text navigation with mono section labels.\n- \"Get started\" CTAs → product verbs (\"Claim space\", \"Release today’s space\", \"Record entry\").\n- Spinners → skeleton rows sized to the real layout.\n- Default shadcn zinc look with 0.5rem radius → a sharp 2px radius system and an offset cyan outline focus.\n- Mega footer → none; the app chrome only.\n\n## 11. Human Fingerprint\n- **Unexpected decision:** the Bay Plate. Every space code, floor and licence plate is drawn as a framed mono chip with a painted-line left rule, the same mark a driver sees on the concrete. It ties the screens to the physical car park.\n- **Radius family / elevation / grid:** sharp, 2px everywhere (inner elements 0px). Zero shadows: depth comes from three surface tints plus an inset hairline, so effectively two elevation steps. 12-column grid with an 8 + 4 content and context-rail split.\n- **Image treatment / icon set:** the only imagery is the live entrance camera frame, shown inside an Inset Well with a 1px Hairline Strong border, 16:9, no rounding, and a mono timestamp overlay bar placed below the frame (not over it). Icons are Lucide at 1.5 stroke, 16/20px.\n",
